"Speed limits, connections per torrent, upload slots and seeding are set for each torrent when you add it, or later under Torrent Settings. Torrents use the proxy from the Connection tab (HTTP or SOCKS5, or the Mac's proxy with \"Use the system settings\") and the speed limit for all downloads. Changes apply to torrents started afterwards. Peers and trackers can see your IP address, or your proxy's." = "E fa'atulaga ai le fa'atapula'a o le saoasaoa, feso'ota'iga i le torrent, slots o le auina atu ma le fa'aputuga mo ia torrent pe a e fa'aopopoina, po'o i le lumana'i i lalo o le Torrent Settings. E fa'aaoga e torrents le proxy mai le Connection tab (HTTP po'o le SOCKS5, po'o le Mac's proxy ma le \"Use the system settings\") ma le fa'atapula'a o le saoasaoa mo uma fa'ataga. E fa'aoga ai suiga mo torrents ua amataina i tua atu. E mafai e tagata fa'aoga ma tagata saili ona va'ai i lau tuatusi IP, po'o lau proxy.";
"Settings used for every download from a website. A site also covers its subdomains (example.com covers www.example.com). Logins are only sent to that site and are kept with the app's other secrets." = "Faʻatonu e faʻaaogaina mo soʻo se faʻaigoaina mai i se 'upega tafaʻilagi. E aofia ai foʻi e se 'upega tafaʻilagi ona subdomains (example.com e aofia ai www.example.com). E tuʻuina atu i lea 'upega tafaʻilagi foʻi faʻamatalaga o le login ma teu faatasi ai ma isi faʻamatalaga tau faʻamatalaga a le polokalama.";
"A backup holds your settings, site settings, queues and the downloads list. Passwords and cookies are never put in a backup." = "O le backup e teu ai au faʻatonu, faʻatonu o le 'upega tafaʻilagi, uaea ma le lisi o faʻaigoa. E le faʻatumu i se backup upu faataga ma kuki.";
"When you copy a link that ends in one of these types, the Add window opens with it." = "Afai e te kope se fesoʻotaʻiga e maeʻa i se tasi o nei ituaiga, o le a tatala le 'Add' window ma ia.";
"Expected checksums are checked automatically when a download finishes. Queues can also quit the app, sleep or shut down the Mac when they are done (Scheduler)." = "E siakiina faʻaautomatika le aofaʻi o suʻega e faʻamoemoeina pe a maeʻa se faʻaigoaina. E mafai foi e le 'Queues' ona taofi le faʻaoga, faʻamalolo pe faʻasese le Mac pe a maeʻa (Scheduler).";
"Save the extension folder, open the browser's extensions page, switch on Developer mode, choose Load unpacked and pick the folder." = "Tuʻu le faila faʻaopoopoga, tatala le itulau o faʻaopoopoga o le browser, faʻaaoga le auala o le tagata atiaʻe, filifili le Faʻapipiʻi faʻatūtū ma filifili le faila.";
"Save the add-on file and drag it onto a Firefox window. Firefox installs add-ons that are signed; see the README for signing your copy." = "Tuʻu le faʻaopoopoga i luga o se Windows Firefox. E faʻapipiʻi e le Firefox faʻaopoopoga ua pasia; tagaʻi i le README mo le pasia o lau kope.";
"Install the ndm command, then for example: ndm https://example.com/file.zip --queue Night" = "Faʻapipiʻi le ndm command, ona mo se faataitaiga: ndm https://example.com/file.zip --queue Night";
"Finding the qualities on offer…" = "O le sailia o le lelei i le ofaina…";
"Video sites are saved in the best quality available, with picture and sound joined." = "O nofoaga o vitio e teu i le lelei sili ona lelei, ma le ata ma le leo faʻatasi.";
"Put a range in square brackets: [001-100] keeps three digits, [1-100] does not, [a-z] uses letters and [0-100:5] counts in fives. Several ranges multiply." = "Tuʻu se vaaiga i totonu o ni faʻamau faʻamau: [001-100] e teuina ai ni numera e tolu, [1-100] e le teuina ai, [a-z] e faʻaaogaina ai ni tusi ma [0-100:5] e faʻanumera ai i ni numera e lima. E faʻatelevaveina ni vaaiga eseese.";
"Explores a website section and lists the files it links to. Only use it on sites you are allowed to download from." = "Faʻaseseina se vaega o le 'upega tafaʻilagi ma faʻaalia ai faila e fesoʻotaʻi atu ai. Faʻaaoga i nofoaga e mafai ona e faʻapipiʻi mai ai.";
